/// A cell of a row in a list or tree with columns.
///
/// Inside a row, between `List::item_begin` and `List::item_end`, call `Cell::begin` for each column you draw, draw
/// the content and call `Cell::end`. Go through the columns from left to right. A column you skip stays empty,
/// and a row that draws no cell spans every column.
#[frame_context]
api Cell {
    /// Starts the cell of the current row in the column with the id `column_id`.
    ///
    /// The cell sits under the header of its column, as wide as the column and as high as a row, and it cuts off
    /// what it holds at its edge. In a tree, the first cell starts after the indent and the arrow.
    ///
    /// `column_id` must be the id of a column in `ListConfig.columns`.
    begin(column_id: u32)
    /// Ends the cell started with `Cell::begin`.
    end()
}
